Third-party components (fetched at build time, not vendored):

- ngtcp2 (https://github.com/ngtcp2/ngtcp2) — MIT License. Statically linked.
- SQLite (https://sqlite.org) — Public domain. Statically linked.
- picotls (https://github.com/h2o/picotls) — MIT License. Statically linked;
  the TLS 1.3 implementation for both TLS-over-TCP and QUIC, via ngtcp2's
  crypto_picotls backend.
- cifra (https://github.com/ctz/cifra) — CC0, and micro-ecc
  (https://github.com/kmackay/micro-ecc) — 2-clause BSD. Statically linked as
  picotls's minicrypto binding.
- Monocypher (https://monocypher.org) — 2-clause BSD or CC-0. Statically
  linked; supplies ED25519 and POLY1305.

None of these impose a relinking obligation, so statically linked binaries —
including proprietary (commercially licensed) distributions — are
unencumbered.

